###
### Certification Catalog endpoints (AC-463)
### Read-only access to the catalog synced from the certification artifact.
### Requires team.sb-environment.edfi-tenant.ods.certification:read on a data store of the team's tenant.
###

### Variables (update these with your values)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3333
@keycloakUrl = https://localhost/auth
@realm = edfi
@teamId = 1
@edfiTenantId = 1

# Machine Client (for M2M authentication)
@machineClientId = edfiadminapp-machine
@machineClientSecret = edfi-machine-secret-456

### 1. Get Machine Token (Client Credentials Flow)
# @name keycloakMachineLogin
POST {{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&client_id={{machineClientId}}
&client_secret={{machineClientSecret}}

###
### Extract machine token from Keycloak response
@machineToken = {{keycloakMachineLogin.response.body.access_token}}

###
### === CATALOG VERSIONS ===
###

### 2. List catalog versions (newest first, no importedAt)
# @name getCatalogVersions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/catalog-versions
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### Capture the first catalog version id for the next requests
@catalogVersionId = {{getCatalogVersions.response.body.$[0].catalogVersionId}}

###
### === AREAS + SCENARIOS ===
###

### 3. Areas with scenarios for one catalog version
# @name getScenarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/scenarios?catalogVersionId={{catalogVersionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### Capture the first scenario id for the steps requests
@scenarioId = {{getScenarios.response.body.$[0].scenarios[0].scenarioId}}

###
### 4. Areas with scenarios across every catalog version (no filter)
# @name getScenariosUnfiltered
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/scenarios
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 5. Unknown catalog version - Should return []
# @name getScenariosUnknownVersion
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/scenarios?catalogVersionId=999999
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### === STEPS + PARAMETERS ===
###

### 6. Steps with parameters for one scenario
# @name getSteps
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/steps?scenarioId={{scenarioId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 7. Steps with parameters for every scenario (no filter)
# @name getStepsUnfiltered
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/steps
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 8. Unknown scenario - Should return []
# @name getStepsUnknownScenario
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/steps?scenarioId=999999
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### === NEGATIVE TESTING SCENARIOS ===
###

### 9. Non-integer catalogVersionId - Should return 400
# @name getScenariosInvalidFilter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/scenarios?catalogVersionId=abc
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 10. Non-integer scenarioId - Should return 400
# @name getStepsInvalidFilter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/steps?scenarioId=abc
Authorization: Bearer {{machineToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 11. No token - Should return 401
# @name getCatalogVersionsNoToken
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/catalog-versions
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 12. Invalid token - Should return 401
# @name getCatalogVersionsInvalidToken
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/edfi-tenants/{{edfiTenantId}}/certification/catalog-versions
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token
Content-Type: application/json
